checklist:[{"text":"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Prove recursive closed shapes, Unicode ordering, invalid dates, malformed identifiers, and cross-platform golden identities","done":true},{"text":"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached","done":true},{"text":"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims","done":true},{"text":"Go native fuzz targets cover scalar parsing and JCS canonicalization at production entry points, with a committed seed corpus derived from the shapes prior reviews found: leap seconds, lowercase RFC3339, Windows reserved device names and wildcards, unpaired surrogates, and duplicate or non-string map keys","done":true},{"text":"Canonicalization is proven round-trip stable and order-independent under fuzz: the identity digest of an object is invariant under key reordering and insignificant whitespace, and no input causes a panic or an accepted value that later refuses","done":true},{"text":"Fuzz runs are bounded and deterministic in the validation suite: a fixed -fuzztime with a seed corpus, so the configured gate stays reproducible rather than time-dependent","done":true},{"text":"Code written per task description and AC","done":true},{"text":"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing","done":true},{"text":"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named","done":true},{"text":"Lint clean","done":true},{"text":"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken","done":true},{"text":"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables","done":true},{"text":"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant","done":true},{"text":"Implementation matches AC","done":true},{"text":"Solution fits project architecture","done":true},{"text":"Tests green","done":true},{"text":"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted","done":true},{"text":"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches","done":true},{"text":"Scoped closed-shape validation exists for Sections 10.1-10.4 and is invoked on the composed production path before identity is calculated or verified: exact top-level and nested member sets, and BlobChunk index/offset/size order, bounds and coverage invariants, with the composed call site named in evidence","done":true},{"text":"Negative tests and fuzz corpus cover an unknown top-level member, an unknown nested member, invalid chunk bounds/order/coverage, and closed Transfer Manifest nested shapes; each must make identity calculation and verification refuse rather than attest","done":true},{"text":"tracecheck -section 17.3 passes for the implemented identity contribution without claiming migration publication or atomic-reference behavior that README correctly reports unavailable","done":true},{"text":"AUDIT, not spot-fix: every open or extension point in closed_shapes.go validates its full key grammar per Section 1.6, and every string[n..m] bound counts Unicode characters rather than UTF-8 bytes; both directions are proven, an invalid key of any namespace is refused and a valid multibyte value at the character bound is accepted","done":true},{"text":"Every fuzz target the candidate defines is invoked by the configured validation suite with a fixed -fuzztime, including the closed-shape target; a newly added target that is not wired into the suite is a gate gap","done":true},{"text":"Constraints are DERIVED from the pinned SPEC.md Sections 10.1-10.4 by systematic enumeration of every declared member type, character bound, nullability, tagged-union, ordering, uniqueness and cross-field rule reachable at this gate, and the enumeration itself is recorded as evidence; a hand-picked subset is not acceptable","done":true},{"text":"Nested value rules reuse the production scalar validators rather than looser local grammars, and the normative TM-GIT-N2 stage-4 refusal plus valid multibyte values at each character limit are proven through both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity","done":true},{"text":"README states only what reproduces through both public identity entries; no completed-audit or coverage claim is made that a reader cannot reproduce","done":true},{"text":"The closed-shape validator is TOTAL over the registered self-identity schema set: every registered schema resolves to a schema-specific shape validator, and a non-circular completeness test derived from the registry fails when any registered schema has no validator, so a newly registered schema cannot silently fall through to extension-only checking","done":true},{"text":"Session Record name is validated against the Section 2.1 term [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63} with a 1-64 character bound, proven through both CalculateObjectIdentity and VerifyObjectIdentity: 64 valid characters accepted; 65 characters, leading hyphen, space, control character and non-ASCII refused","done":true},{"text":"A per-member constraint enumeration artifact carries one row for every declared member of Session Record, Blob Descriptor and Transfer Manifest including nested closed types, each naming its enforcing call site, with member lists derived from the requireExactMembers argument lists so artifact and code cannot drift; a member with no constraint beyond its type says so explicitly and quotes the spec text","done":true},{"text":"The manifest entry case-collision check is linear rather than quadratic, with a measured regression guard: a well-formed 65536-entry workspace_tree Transfer Manifest that fits the identity size cap must not take seconds at the identity gate","done":true},{"text":"constraint-enumeration.md claims only what the suite proves: every row asserting a bound is enforced exactly as declared is backed by an executable boundary case, or the row states plainly that production enforces it while no test pins it","done":true},{"text":"The single publicly unreachable bound GitIndex.entries is documented with its measured encoded size, proven refused by the identity size cap, and covered by a direct validator-level boundary test with the production call site named; the other 22 bounds are proven through both public entries","done":true},{"text":"The attached rev11 mutation sweep is re-run in full over every bound expression, not just the 15 named rows, and it reports ZERO surviving mutants; the sweep output is attached as evidence and each closed bound has accept-at-bound and refuse-past-bound cases through both identity entries","done":true},{"text":"The rev12 reviewer harness genmutants.py is re-run over the whole production file including constant declarations, not only call sites, and reports zero actionable survivors; its output is attached as evidence","done":true},{"text":"The trailing zero-size BlobChunk clause has its own boundary case that reaches closed_shapes.go:614 rather than being short-circuited by the empty-descriptor rule, and the constraint-enumeration row stops claiming it is subsumed","done":false}]
